Package: quickremote-pc
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Berat Kaan Akcan <beratkaanakcan@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6, libstdc++6, libgtk-3-0, libx11-6, libxi6, python3
Recommends: python3-uno, avahi-daemon, pkexec | policykit-1
Suggests: libreoffice-impress
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/berat-kaan-akcan/QuickRemote
Description: QuickRemote PC: control presentations from your phone
 The computer side of QuickRemote. The QuickRemote phone app connects to it
 over the local network and controls LibreOffice Impress and WPS
 Presentation slideshows (next and previous slide, laser, pen, black screen),
 the mouse, media and volume.
 .
 Installing the package adds a udev rule that lets the logged-in user use
 /dev/uinput (the virtual keyboard and mouse); removing it takes the rule away.
